      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the equation of the line passing through the points \\((2,2,1)\\) and \\((5,1,-2)\\). The parametric equations of the line can be written as follows:\n\n\\[\nx = 2 + 3t\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 2 - t\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 1 - 3t\n\\]\n\nWe are given that a point on this line has an \\(x\\)-coordinate of 4. We need to find the corresponding \\(z\\)-coordinate for this point.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = 4\\) into the parametric equation for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4 = 2 + 3t\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(t\\):\n\n\\[\n4 - 2 = 3t\n\\]\n\\[\n2 = 3t\n\\]\n\\[\nt = \\frac{2}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(t = \\frac{2}{3}\\) into the parametric equation for \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\nz = 1 - 3t\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 1 - 3 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 1 - 2\n\\]\n\\[\nz = -1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the \\(z\\)-coordinate of the point is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
